nd feedback to further undertake teaching, research, and extension activities with National perspectives.<\/p>","slug":"college-of-fisheries","org_state_id":19,"org_district_id":378,"org_block_id":null,"org_type":"Knowledge Institutions","specialization":[1,5],"created_on":"2025-10-06 15:11:33","updated_on":"2025-10-16 21:27:53","org_state_name":"Madhya Pradesh","org_district_name":"Datia","org_block_name":"","events":{"count":2,"data":[{"id":213848,"user_id":71532197,"event_name":"Khelo India Samvaad","description":"<p>Khelo India Samvaad \u2013 Khel Ki Baat PM ke Saath is a nationwide youth engagement programme being organised by Mera Yuva Bharat (MY Bharat) under the Department of Youth Affairs, Ministry of Youth Affairs and Sports, on the occasion of National Sports Day 2026. The programme aims to bring together young people from across the country to celebrate India\u2019s growing sporting culture and participate in a national conversation on the future of sports and youth-led nationbuilding. The programme will be organised simultaneously in selected colleges across districts of the country. Participants will witness a virtual address by the Hon\u2019ble Prime Minister, followed by a local programme featuring interactions with sportspersons and public representatives. A key part of the programme is the Yuva Samvaad, where young people will have the opportunity to share their ideas, perspectives and aspirations on important themes such as strengthening the sports ecosystem, nurturing talent for the 2036 Olympics, building youth leadership and participation, and empowering young people for Viksit Bharat. Participants can also submit their suggestions digitally through the MY Bharat Suggestions Box. The programme provides a platform for youth to learn from inspiring sporting journeys, share their own perspectives and contribute to discussions on how sport can build leadership, discipline, resilience and a stronger future for India.\u00a0<\/p><p>Join the Khelo India Samvaad and be part of the conversation shaping India\u2019s sporting future.\u00a0<\/p><p>Venue: Rani Lakshmi Bai Central Agricultural University, Datia Campus<\/p><p>Date: 27 August 2026\u00a0<\/p><p>Apply Now<\/p>","numer_of_days":null,"event_from_date":"2026-08-27","event_to_date":"2026-08-27","last_rsvp_date":null,"state_id":19,"city_id":378,"block_id":3808,"image_path":"6a8f9bca1bade213848.jpeg","eventHighlights":null,"event_address":"College of Fisheries, RLBCAU, Datia Campus","specialization":"136","nyf_category":0,"nyf_activity_type":null,"nyf_component_type":null,"org_id":122379,"created_at":"2026-08-27 02:07:05","state":"Madhya Pradesh","district":"Datia","nyf_category_name":"","getnyfeventactivity":[],"getnyfeventcomponent":[]},{"id":211878,"user_id":71532197,"event_name":"National Sports Day 2026","description":"<p>The College of Fisheries, Rani Lakshmibai Central Agricultural University (RLBCAU), Datia Campus, will celebrate <b>National Sports Day<\/b> on <b>29th August 2026<\/b> with enthusiasm and sportsmanship. National Sports Day commemorates the birth anniversary of Major Dhyan Chand, the legendary Indian hockey player, and highlights the importance of sports in promoting physical fitness, mental well-being, discipline, teamwork, leadership, and a healthy lifestyle. The celebration will encourage students to actively participate in sports and develop a spirit of healthy competition and camaraderie. As part of the celebration, Badminton and Table Tennis matches will be organized for boys and girls in singles and doubles categories, providing students an opportunity to showcase their talent and sporting spirit.<\/p>","numer_of_days":null,"event_from_date":"2026-08-29","event_to_date":"2026-08-29","last_rsvp_date":null,"state_id":19,"city_id":378,"block_id":3808,"image_path":"6a8d43ec1a171211878.jpg","eventHighlights":null,"event_address":"College of Fisheries, RLBCAU, Datia Campus","specialization":"136","nyf_category":0,"nyf_activity_type":null,"