nternship<\/b> is organized by the <b>Department of Cyber Security, Government Holkar (Model Autonomous) Science College, Indore<\/b>, in collaboration with <b>Marcraft, an NPI Brand and AIIPL<\/b>. The internship is designed to provide participants with foundational knowledge, practical understanding, and hands-on exposure to Cyber Security. The programme covers key concepts related to cyber security, common cyber threats and attacks, basic security techniques, network and internet security, cyber hygiene, privacy and data protection, phishing and social engineering awareness, secure browsing, Wi-Fi and email security, and safe online transactions.<\/p><p>Participants will learn about the importance and goals of Cyber Security, the CIA Triad, vulnerabilities and risks, and different types of cyber attacks. The programme covers common threats such as malware, viruses, worms, Trojans, ransomware, phishing, social engineering, password attacks, Denial of Service (DoS), spoofing, and email security.<\/p><p>The internship also focuses on practical security practices including password security, authentication and authorization, Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA), access control, data security, data backup, basic encryption, firewall concepts, antivirus and endpoint security, system updates, and cyber hygiene.<\/p><p>Participants will further explore network and internet security, secure browsing, HTTP and HTTPS, Wi-Fi security, public Wi-Fi risks, safe email practices, phishing identification, secure social media practices, and safe online transactions.<\/p><p>The internship includes guided practical activities such as analyzing sample phishing emails, identifying suspicious links and attachments, checking website security, configuring password and MFA settings, practicing safe browsing, identifying social engineering techniques, and preparing a Cyber Security Awareness Report.<\/p>","numer_of_days":null,"event_from_date":"2026-09-01","event_to_date":"2026-09-06","last_r